I have a complete picture. Here is my report.

## Summary

The repository is Spring PetClinic REST converted to OfficeFloor function injection. The key finding: **there is a failing/unimplemented requirement** — an acceptance test expects a `GOLD` membership tier for 3+ member households, but the current tier computation only ever returns `SILVER` or `BRONZE`.

## 1. Membership tier computation

**File:** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`

The tier is a derived field computed at mapping time (Owner → OwnerDto), lines 24-25 and 56-64:

```java
@Mapping(target = "membershipTier", expression = "java(membershipTier(owner))")
...
/**
 * Derive the membership tier: 'SILVER' when the owner has no namesakes
 * (namesakeCount is 0) and an email is present, otherwise 'BRONZE'.
 */
default String membershipTier(Owner owner) {
    boolean unique = Integer.valueOf(0).equals(owner.getNamesakeCount());
    boolean hasEmail = owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isEmpty();
    return unique && hasEmail ? "SILVER" : "BRONZE";
}
```

Note: this method has **no access to `OwnerRepository`** and there is **no GOLD branch**. It only reads `namesakeCount` and `email` off the entity. GOLD (3+ household members) is not computed anywhere. `MembershipTier` is not an enum — tiers are bare strings. No `GOLD` string exists anywhere in `/src/main`.

The OpenAPI spec (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml`, ~line 2132) documents `membershipTier` only as SILVER/BRONZE — it also does not mention GOLD.

## 2. Owner creation flow — POST /owners

**YAML:** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`

Guarded by `authorize: "hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')"`. Every step carries `govern: [ transaction ]`. Pipeline order: `validate → normalizeAddress → normalizeTelephone → ensureUniqueTelephone → ensureUniqueHousehold → ensureCityHasCapacity → ensureDailyLimit → normalizeEmail → build → resolveRegistrationDate → assignCustomerCode → assignHousehold → countNamesakes → flagBulkSignup → save → audit → respond`.

**Function classes** in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/`. Most relevant to membership/household:

- `AssignHouseholdId.java` — sets `householdId` via `HouseholdKey.id(lastName, address)` (SHA-256 hex of the normalized last name + address). Runs before save.
- `CountNamesakes.java` — iterates `ownerRepository.findAll()`, counts case-insensitive first+last name matches, stores via `owner.setNamesakeCount(count)`. This is the pattern the membership tier's `namesakeCount` depends on. (This shows the established idiom for deriving-and-storing a count at create time.)
- `EnsureUniqueHousehold.java` — rejects (409 `DuplicateHouseholdException`) a create whose last name+address collide with an existing owner **unless** `request.getSharesHousehold()` is true.
- `BuildOwner.java` — maps `OwnerFieldsDto` → `Owner` via `OwnerMapper.toOwner(request)`.
- `ValidateNewOwner.java` — reads `@RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` (the single body-binding step), validates required fields, republishes via `Out<OwnerFieldsDto>`.
- `FlagBulkSignup.java` — uses `DailyRegistrations.countOn(...)` iterating `findAll()`; the same iterate-findAll pattern.
- `SaveOwner.java` — `ownerRepository.save(owner)`.
- `RespondWithOwnerCreated.java` — maps to `OwnerDto` via `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner)` and returns 201 Created.

**Helper (household key):** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/HouseholdKey.java` — package-private `final` util. `of(lastName, address)` = normalized `lastName + ' ' + address` (trim, collapse whitespace, lowercase); `id(...)` = SHA-256 hex of that key. Two owners of the same household get the same stable `householdId`.

## 3. Owner entity

**File:** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java` (extends `Person`)

Persistent fields (JPA `@Column`): `address`, `city`, `telephone` (E.164 pattern), `email`, `registrationDate` (LocalDate), `customerCode`, **`householdId` (String, `@Column(name="household_id")`, lines 60-61)**, `namesakeCount` (Integer), `bulkSignupWarning` (Boolean), and `pets` (`@OneToMany`, EAGER). Standard getters/setters for each (e.g. `getHouseholdId()`/`setHouseholdId()` lines 120-126). **There is no stored "household member count" field and no `membershipTier`/tier field** — household membership is represented only by the shared `householdId` string; members are not otherwise linked.

## 4. OwnerRepository

**File:** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/OwnerRepository.java`

Interface methods only:
- `Collection<Owner> findByLastName(String lastName)`
- `Page<Owner> findByLastName(String lastName, Pageable)`
- `Owner findById(int id)`
- `void save(Owner owner)`
- `Collection<Owner> findAll()`
- `Page<Owner> findAll(Pageable)`
- `void delete(Owner owner)`

**No `householdId`-based query and no member-count method.** Existing create-pipeline rules (CountNamesakes, EnsureUniqueHousehold, DailyRegistrations) all derive counts by iterating `findAll()` in-memory — that is the established pattern any household-size computation would follow.

## 5. Tests

**Failing/target test:** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java`

```java
/** tier-gold: membershipTier is 'GOLD' when the owner's household has 3+ members after this
 * create. Build a shared household (same lastName + address, sharesHousehold) and assert the third
 * member is GOLD. */
@Test
void coreGoldForThreeMemberHousehold() throws Exception {
    String lastName = uniqueLastName();
    String address = uniqueAddress();
    for (int i = 0; i < 2; i++) {
        ObjectNode m = ownerNode();
        m.put("lastName", lastName);
        m.put("address", address);
        m.put("sharesHousehold", true);
        createOwnerOk(m);
    }
    ObjectNode third = ownerNode();
    third.put("lastName", lastName); third.put("address", address);
    third.put("sharesHousehold", true);
    int id = createOwnerOk(third);
    getOwner(id).andExpect(jsonPath("$.membershipTier").value("GOLD"));
}
```

**Base helper:** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java` — MockMvc-based (`@AutoConfigureMockMvc`). Relevant helpers: `ownerNode()` (lines 117-125; builds a valid owner with firstName "Test", **no email set**), `createOwnerOk()` (POST /api/owners, expects 2xx, returns id), `getOwner(int)` (GET /api/owners/{id}). Note `ownerNode()` omits email, so under current logic all three household members would be BRONZE (no email) — the test expects GOLD regardless.

### Key gap for implementation
To satisfy the GOLD test, `membershipTier` must become GOLD when the owner's household (owners sharing the same `householdId`) has 3+ members. Since `OwnerMapper` has no repository access and Owner has no stored member-count, this needs either: (a) a stored household-member-count field on `Owner` populated at create time by a new pipeline step (mirroring `CountNamesakes` — iterate `findAll()` matching `householdId`), then read in `membershipTier`; or (b) giving the tier computation repository access. The existing codebase strongly favors pattern (a) — a stored count computed via a create-pipeline function iterating `findAll()`. The GOLD branch must also take precedence over the existing SILVER/BRONZE logic.

